From 7656a16eae6b99e3ae2672c98db9faf713816e71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:23:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U10: church-year rules and the generated family year map

scripts/lib/church-year.mjs computes the church year from rules: Easter by
the computus (checked against an independent algorithm for 1583 to 4099),
Ash Wednesday, Palm Sunday and Holy Week, Pentecost, Advent Sunday, the
twelve days of Christmas, Epiphany, All Saints, and US Thanksgiving. A week
runs Sunday to Saturday and keeps the season of its Sunday; a feast claims
the plain week it falls in.

scripts/build-family-year.mjs writes client/src/lib/familyYear.generated.ts
for church years 2026 to 2031 (to November 29, 2031): the seasons, the days
each daily set in family-seasonal.json runs (Advent stays December 1 to 25),
and the devotion for every week. Set seasons are served by their set; every
other week takes the next Foundations devotion in a rotation counted from
Advent Sunday 2026, so all of them are used and moving the map's first year
never reshuffles it. Hand pins live in client/public/family-year-overrides.json
and do not use up a rotation slot. client/src/lib/familyYear.ts reads the map
(week, season, set day for a date; the reader's local date) with no network.

CI runs build-family-year --check after validate-family: it fails when the
committed map is stale, an input has a problem, or fewer than twelve months
remain. server/church-year.test.ts holds the known dates (Advent Sunday
2026-11-29; Easter 2027-03-28; Ash Wednesday 2027-02-10; Pentecost
2027-05-16), the no-op regeneration, and the horizon.

